\item \strong{Model III} (radius-distance model; Okada & Imaizumi, 1987): \code{c(j, k) = r_j}, the radius of a circle (sphere, hypersphere) centered at \code{x_j}.
\item \strong{Model I}: the most general model, in which \code{c} depends on the pair of
objects and the dimension. It is not implemented yet, because how it is
restricted to be estimable is given only in Okada and Imaizumi (1984).
